#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:2
msgid "Using Subordinate Nodes (C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:4
msgid ""
"**Goal:** Learn how to create and use subordinate nodes "
"(``create_sub_node``) in ``rclcpp`` to organize topics and services "
"hierarchically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:6
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Intermediate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:8
msgid "**Time:** 10 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:12
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:15
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:17
msgid ""
"A **subordinate node** (or **sub-node**) is a secondary node instance "
"created from an existing ``rclcpp::Node`` via ``create_sub_node()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:18
msgid ""
"Sub-nodes share the parent node's underlying context, executor callbacks, "
"parameter interface, logging interface, and ROS graph identity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:19
msgid ""
"Sub-nodes define an additional relative **sub-namespace** that scopes "
"entities (publishers, subscriptions, service clients, and service servers) "
"created through them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:20
msgid ""
"In ROS 1, developers often used ``ros::NodeHandle`` instances to scope "
"namespaces for internal helper classes; in ROS 2, ``create_sub_node()`` "
"fulfills a similar role for C++ components within a node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:23
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:25
msgid ""
"In ROS 2, a standard node represents a single entity in the computation "
"graph. However, complex nodes frequently contain internal helper libraries, "
"device sub-drivers, or modular algorithms that need to publish or subscribe "
"to topics under their own scoped namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:28
msgid ""
"Creating a full separate node for each internal subcomponent incurs "
"overhead: each node has its own middleware participant and discovery entity, "
"requires separate executor management or thread scheduling, and clutters the "
"node graph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:30
msgid ""
"To solve this, ``rclcpp::Node`` provides the ``create_sub_node()`` method. A "
"subordinate node allows internal components within a single ROS 2 node "
"process to encapsulate their own relative topic and service namespaces while "
"reusing all of the parent node's underlying resources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:34
msgid "How Subordinate Nodes Work"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:37
msgid "Namespaces and naming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:39
msgid ""
"When you create a sub-node, you provide a relative sub-namespace string:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:41
msgid ""
"auto node = std::make_shared<rclcpp::Node>(\"my_node\", \"/my_ns\");\n"
"auto sub_node = node->create_sub_node(\"sub_ns\");"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:46
msgid "The node provides three namespace-related query methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:48
msgid ""
"``get_namespace()``: Returns the parent node's base namespace (for example, "
"``\"/my_ns\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:49
msgid ""
"``get_sub_namespace()``: Returns the accumulated relative sub-namespace (for "
"example, ``\"sub_ns\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:50
msgid ""
"``get_effective_namespace()``: Returns the concatenation of the base "
"namespace and the accumulated sub-namespace (for example, ``\"/my_ns/"
"sub_ns\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:52
msgid "Sub-nodes can also be nested hierarchically:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:54
msgid ""
"auto sub_node2 = sub_node->create_sub_node(\"nested\");\n"
"// sub_node2->get_sub_namespace()       -> \"sub_ns/nested\"\n"
"// sub_node2->get_effective_namespace() -> \"/my_ns/sub_ns/nested\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:61
msgid "Entity scoping rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:63
msgid ""
"When you use a sub-node to create publishers, subscriptions, service "
"clients, or service servers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:65
msgid ""
"**Relative names**: Any relative topic or service name (a name not starting "
"with ``/``) is resolved relative to the sub-node's *effective namespace*. "
"For example, creating a publisher for ``\"chatter\"`` on a sub-node with "
"effective namespace ``\"/my_ns/sub_ns\"`` results in the topic ``\"/my_ns/"
"sub_ns/chatter\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:67
msgid ""
"**Absolute names**: Any absolute name (starting with ``/``) bypasses all "
"namespaces and resolves directly to the global name, identical to standard "
"ROS 2 naming behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:68
msgid ""
"**Relative requirement**: The sub-namespace passed to ``create_sub_node()`` "
"must be relative (it cannot start with ``/`` and cannot be empty). Passing "
"an absolute or empty sub-namespace throws "
"``rclcpp::exceptions::NameValidationError``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:72
msgid "Shared resources vs. Scoped behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:74
msgid ""
"The following table summarizes what is shared with the parent node and what "
"is scoped by the subordinate node:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:80
msgid "Aspect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:81
msgid "Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:82
msgid "**Graph identity**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:83
msgid ""
"Shared. The sub-node shares the parent's "
"``rclcpp::node_interfaces::NodeBaseInterface``. It does not appear as a "
"separate node in ``ros2 node list``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:86
msgid "**Node name**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:87
msgid "Shared. ``sub_node->get_name()`` returns the parent node's name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:89
msgid "**Executor and callbacks**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:90
msgid ""
"Shared. Callbacks registered on sub-node entities are dispatched by the "
"parent node's executor. You spin the parent node, not the sub-node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:93
msgid "**Parameters**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:94
msgid ""
"Shared. The sub-node shares the parent's "
"``rclcpp::node_interfaces::NodeParametersInterface``. Declaring or querying "
"parameters operates on the parent node's parameter store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:97
msgid "**Logging**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:98
msgid ""
"Shared. The sub-node shares the parent's "
"``rclcpp::node_interfaces::NodeLoggingInterface`` and parent logger."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:100
msgid "**Clock and timers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:101
msgid "Shared. Timers and clock interfaces are shared with the parent node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:103
msgid "**Entity namespaces**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:104
msgid ""
"Scoped. Relative publishers, subscriptions, and services use the sub-node's "
"effective namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:108
msgid "C++ Example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:110
msgid ""
"The following example demonstrates creating a parent node and two "
"subordinate nodes to publish telemetry from two sensors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:112
msgid ""
"#include <chrono>\n"
"#include <memory>\n"
"#include <string>\n"
"\n"
"#include \"rclcpp/rclcpp.hpp\"\n"
"#include \"std_msgs/msg/string.hpp\"\n"
"\n"
"using namespace std::chrono_literals;\n"
"\n"
"class RobotSystemNode : public rclcpp::Node\n"
"{\n"
"public:\n"
"  RobotSystemNode()\n"
"  : Node(\"robot_system\", \"robot\")\n"
"  {\n"
"    // Create subordinate nodes for distinct subsystems\n"
"    imu_subnode_ = this->create_sub_node(\"imu\");\n"
"    camera_subnode_ = this->create_sub_node(\"camera\");\n"
"\n"
"    RCLCPP_INFO(\n"
"      this->get_logger(),\n"
"      \"Parent node namespace: %s, effective: %s\",\n"
"      this->get_namespace(),\n"
"      this->get_effective_namespace().c_str());\n"
"\n"
"    RCLCPP_INFO(\n"
"      this->get_logger(),\n"
"      \"IMU sub-node sub_ns: %s, effective: %s\",\n"
"      imu_subnode_->get_sub_namespace().c_str(),\n"
"      imu_subnode_->get_effective_namespace().c_str());\n"
"\n"
"    RCLCPP_INFO(\n"
"      this->get_logger(),\n"
"      \"Camera sub-node sub_ns: %s, effective: %s\",\n"
"      camera_subnode_->get_sub_namespace().c_str(),\n"
"      camera_subnode_->get_effective_namespace().c_str());\n"
"\n"
"    // Create publishers via subordinate nodes using relative topic names\n"
"    // Resolved topics will be /robot/imu/data and /robot/camera/status\n"
"    imu_pub_ = imu_subnode_-"
">create_publisher<std_msgs::msg::String>(\"data\", 10);\n"
"    camera_pub_ = camera_subnode_-"
">create_publisher<std_msgs::msg::String>(\"status\", 10);\n"
"\n"
"    timer_ = this->create_wall_timer(\n"
"      1000ms, std::bind(&RobotSystemNode::publish_data, this));\n"
"  }\n"
"\n"
"private:\n"
"  void publish_data()\n"
"  {\n"
"    auto imu_msg = std_msgs::msg::String();\n"
"    imu_msg.data = \"imu_ok\";\n"
"    imu_pub_->publish(imu_msg);\n"
"\n"
"    auto cam_msg = std_msgs::msg::String();\n"
"    cam_msg.data = \"camera_streaming\";\n"
"    camera_pub_->publish(cam_msg);\n"
"  }\n"
"\n"
"  rclcpp::Node::SharedPtr imu_subnode_;\n"
"  rclcpp::Node::SharedPtr camera_subnode_;\n"
"  rclcpp::Publisher<std_msgs::msg::String>::SharedPtr imu_pub_;\n"
"  rclcpp::Publisher<std_msgs::msg::String>::SharedPtr camera_pub_;\n"
"  rclcpp::TimerBase::SharedPtr timer_;\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"int main(int argc, char * argv[])\n"
"{\n"
"  rclcpp::init(argc, argv);\n"
"  auto node = std::make_shared<RobotSystemNode>();\n"
"  rclcpp::spin(node);\n"
"  rclcpp::shutdown();\n"
"  return 0;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:189
msgid "Verifying Behavior with CLI Tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:191
msgid ""
"When running this node, you can verify how subordinate nodes appear in the "
"ROS 2 graph using the standard command-line tools:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:193
msgid "List the active nodes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:195
msgid ""
"$ ros2 node list\n"
"/robot/robot_system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:200
msgid ""
"Notice that only the parent node ``/robot/robot_system`` appears in the "
"graph. The subordinate nodes do not register as separate nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:203
msgid "List the active topics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:205
msgid ""
"$ ros2 topic list\n"
"/parameter_events\n"
"/robot/camera/status\n"
"/robot/imu/data\n"
"/rosout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:213
msgid ""
"The topics published by the subordinate nodes are correctly scoped under ``/"
"robot/camera/`` and ``/robot/imu/`` according to each sub-node's effective "
"namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:216
msgid "When to Use Subordinate Nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:218
msgid ""
"**Use subordinate nodes** when you are developing modular C++ classes or "
"internal helper libraries within a single executable and want each component "
"to manage its own scoped topic or service namespace without the overhead of "
"additional ROS 2 nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:219
msgid ""
"**Use composable nodes (components)** when your components represent "
"independent units of computation that should be independently discoverable, "
"dynamically loaded into component containers at launch or runtime, or "
"composed into separate processes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/Using-Sub-Nodes.rst:220
msgid ""
"**Use standalone nodes** when components require independent operating "
"system processes, distinct lifecycles, or physical isolation across machines."
msgstr ""
